WEBVTT

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.000
Christian Era 2599

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.000
Aki, what are you doing?

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.250
Come over here and eat with us.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.020
No way in hell!

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.870
That's a moth, isn't it?

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.580
Silkworms.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.040
They're pretty good once 
you get used to them.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.150
Still not happening.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.500
Your base is a silk moth, too, isn't it?

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.850
So it's your friend.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.100
All the more reason why I can't!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.400
Jeez. No one likes pushy men.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.660
Now, now, Aki-chan.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.660
But we got closer 
 because of a moth, as well.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.760
Was it?

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.740
Yeah. A moth got into the room

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.050
so I ran out, and you 
said, "L-Leave it to me!"

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.550
That's right. And ever since then...

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.200
<i>The body itself</i>

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.540
<i>isn't important.</i>

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.480
Shokichi, let's go.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.970
Those things are going 
to start attacking soon.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:07.990
Right.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.210
Aki-chan...

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.710
I'm so sorry.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.490
<i>What's important is</i>

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.360
<i>that we survive.</i>

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:27.980
<i>I...</i>

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.480
<i>left you behind.</i>

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.160
<b><i>On Track and Reckless</i></b>

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.800
Captain...

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.400
What's the matter?

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.560
This is the arena you picked, isn't it?

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:58.500
You've gotten weak.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.710
You're not gonna run?

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.030
Not that I'd let you get away, anyway.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.460
You're in my class, aren't you?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.180
What are you doing in front of your house?

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.790
Did a cockroach pop up in 
your room or something?

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.660
A moth...

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:24.610
Shokichi!

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.840
<i>Aki-chan...</i>

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.840
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.520
Captured.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.710
Are you all in one piece, Keiji?

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:25.210
Wow... You're amazing, Captain.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.710
You did a pretty good job yourself.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.000
Seriously though... 
Being in U-NASA for twenty years,

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.100
how many times did you go through 
the surgery to get like that?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.600
How many times?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.080
What are you talking about?

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.730
I only have the Japanese giant hornet.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:43.570
Wha? But you just defeated like 
a hundred of them... right?

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.270
Like from noon on...

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.350
Well, I am a hornet.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.650
But you, like, spit out poison, 
and shoot poison stingers.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:51.980
Hornet.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.410
And your arm strength is pretty...

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.680
Hornet.

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:56.250
The things coming out of your elbows..

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:57.910
Those are the hornet's mandibles.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.290
And...

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.790
Looking so awesome is one of the 
hornet's special qualities.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.050
What the heck?

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:05.920
Ow...

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.790
Now, what to do.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.260
We have to get back up.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.240
Right.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:04.950
Ivan-kun, what are you looking 
at that's making you so red?

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.850
Uh, well, um...

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.330
Alexander-senpai was just...

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:11.780
Huh? What? Sorry, I wasn't looking.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.740
You totally pointed!

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.360
Strange...

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:21.620
Apparently this facility might 
not be so important after all.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:22.870
Eh?

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:27.000
Ivan-kun. Name one current 
unnatural circumstance.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.500
Nothing's come after us.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.310
Precisely.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:35.260
Not only is nothing pursuing us, 
but nothing was guarding this place, either.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.370
Considering they knew we 
were coming from Earth,

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.890
it is entirely too unnatural.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:44.270
Um... If this really isn't 
an important facility,

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.440
what's going to happen to our mission?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.150
That's not going to change.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:55.650
Right. What's important is that 
it's sparked our interest.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.160
As far as I know, <i>that</i> is definitely here.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:06.910
Apparently Rahab's intent and the 
Terraformars' intent is not the same.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:11.320
Look.

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:20.670
This is already some fantasy 
considering how far cockroaches

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.940
have evolved in five hundred years,

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:27.960
but it's only been twenty 
years since Bugs 2.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.070
I wonder if all of Mars's 
silkworms are like this.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.860
Who knows?

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.240
Hopefully it's just around here, but...

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.510
Anyway, we're going to investigate.

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.010
It's finally over.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:09.040
For now. So, you can shoot strings.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:12.980
And you're not too bad 
with that stick, either.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:18.170
Yeah... But I can only produce 
one, and it's not long.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:21.930
Also, there's nothing special about 
being able to use a stick.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.120
This is just some thug using his pipe.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.320
You're not even out of breath this time.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:29.500
Even after you handled all of those.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.500
Well... that time was...

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.050
What?

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.300
Something in the sky just now...

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.240
Eh?

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.440
How about this?

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.050
What's this?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:04.300
I see. So this isn't where those 
things live or their place of worship.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.200
This is where they store things.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:11.930
This isn't Bugs... is it? This shape is...

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.210
Huh?

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:16.670
Great Carp Number 3.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:18.430
A hundred years ago,

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:21.420
it was the first unmanned vessel 
that we lost contact with.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:27.150
What the roaches have their 
hands on are the guns,

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:31.180
vehicles, textiles, and 
medicine that was on Bugs.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:34.060
That's what we thought, but...

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:38.000
They'd actually found 
something much earlier.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:43.200
An even more powerful tool to fight with.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.630
Is something wrong, Keiji?

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.260
Oh, well...

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:55.250
I was just wondering how this thing was

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.840
planning to get back up there after it defeated us.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:02.380
Sorry for saying something stupid.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:03.340
No...

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:13.030
<i>It's true that these things have 
been acting a bit unnatural.</i>

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.170
<i>What is it?</i>

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:25.860
<i>The fighting tool that the Terraformars 
had obtained previously...</i>

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:27.530
<i>That is...</i>

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:32.480
<i>The fuel systems that were to 
be used to go back to Earth.</i>

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.230
<i>Meaning...</i>

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:04.490
What is this?

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.780
Marcos! Sanjo-san!

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.450
Hey, everyone!

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.700
Why you...

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.450
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.960
Damn it... What is this?

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.090
Damn it!

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:25.090
Everyone! Marcos! Kanako!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:25.920
Yo!

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:29.800
We're safe! I think those 
things probably missed.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.600
But the flames are bad.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.060
Seriously?

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.710
At a time like this?

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.480
Marcos! The medicine!

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.000
D-Damn it! I can't die!

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:07.840
S-Someone!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.430
Wha...

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.970
H-Hey... I know you guys came 
here as a giant group, but...

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:41.930
Sorry, we've been fighting since noon 
and the medicine's already... out.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:51.680
Th-This is a bit too difficult...

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:01.770
<i>If you pick up a gun, figuring out how
 to pull the trigger is pretty intuitive.</i>

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:04.300
<i>If they're that intelligent,</i>

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:07.490
<i>it's even plausible to think 
that they could drive a car.</i>

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.690
<i>However, this is just...</i>

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.040
I-Is this...

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.520
Yeah, it is.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.420
Out of all the countries that 
participated in Annex 1,

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.020
one of them has...

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.900
<i>...betrayed us.</i>

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:50.900
<i>Who is it?!</i>

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.340
A-Apparently there's nothing else I can do.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:10.180
Y-You guys should have come the other day.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.470
Major leaguer.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.810
Dead on. Next...

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.020
I'm here to save you, you bastard.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:34.810
<b>12th</b>

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.650
<b>Alex K. Stewart</b>

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.650
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 12th</b>

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.030
<b>Alex K. Stewart</b>

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.030
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 12th</b>

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.660
<b>Alex K. Stewart</b>

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.660
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 12th</b>

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:44.500
<i>There is a physical ability 
used for fighting that</i>

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.000
<i>humanity did not lose over 
the course of evolution.</i>

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:50.790
<i>And that is...</i>

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:54.550
<i>throwing!</i>

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:03.600
<i>Wait... is he throwing under the 
assumption that I'm transformed?!</i>

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:06.270
Wait!

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.150
Time! Time!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.560
That bastard!

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.150
As soon as we regroup, I'm going to...

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.160
...kiss the bastard!

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.040
All right!

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:37.140
Here it comes, here it comes.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.180
Here it comes, here it comes, here it comes.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:42.700
Here it comes, here it comes, here it comes!

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.710
We're playing baseball, even on Mars?

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.230
Well, I guess I'll just 
have to play with you.

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:54.730
Since I'm the only one

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.570
who can react to one of your balls.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.210
Well, here's another one 
with an interesting shape.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.450
Take off that mitt.

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:23.290
Erika, are you safe?

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.470
Y-Yes...

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:27.730
Just stay right there.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.320
<i>I just saw it...</i>

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:36.230
<i>Just for a moment. Something that looked 
like its whole body was a mirror...</i>

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:39.650
<i>Wh-Where is it?</i>

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.400
<i>I know it just...</i>

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:52.330
Crap! It's going to open the bug cages!

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.610
Ow...

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.280
Marcos.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:23.450
H-Hey... I guess I made it in time.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.010
It's right over there.

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:30.950
One more of those...

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:32.520
It'll be fine.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.710
There's something amazing 
in the No. 2 Division.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:36.960
Alex!

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.550
Righto!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.100
Commander...

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.220
I-I'm sorry.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:10.780
W-We...

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:14.670
Th-There were so many victims...

00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:16.750
Well done enduring it.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:19.800
You've captured a lot.

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:24.310
Jared, Erika.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:26.260
Leave the rest to me.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.830
Sorry to keep you waiting, 
you roachy bastards.

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:58.960
Now, let's settle the matter of

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:02.530
which one of us is the vermin.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:40.320
<b><i>This Way and That Way</i></b>
